<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_ScaldSteamLock.xml    UtinniPatches · authored 2026-09-13, reworked 2026-09-18
  ============================================================================
  SCALD_MECHANICS_1 build pass, S1 "the boil layer — standing steam" (spec
  §S1: "the ruled RM_GameCondition_EnvironmentalWeather... as a permanent
  biomeMapConditions entry... forced RUT_ScaldSteam... configured clear
  spells (§9's 'still day' that shows the wrecks). No damage fields — the
  steam is clean; the WATER burns.").

  🔴 2026-09-18 SUPERSEDES the 2026-09-13 build: the prior pass shipped
  `GameCondition_EnvironmentalWeather` + `EnvironmentalWeatherExtension`
  (forcedWeather only) and flagged "configured clear spells" as an honest
  gap, since that class's `ForcedWeather()` returns `ext.forcedWeather`
  UNCONDITIONALLY with no periodic-lapse hook, and adding one would change
  shared behaviour every other kit consuming that exact class depends on.
  That gap is now closed WITHOUT touching the shared class at all: reused
  `RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_GameCondition_WeatherPulse` +
  `WeatherPulseExtension` instead — the class FORGE_MECHANICS_1's F1 pass
  already shipped and compiled (`RUT_ForgePulse.xml` is the live sibling
  consumer). That class is symmetric by construction: "force `baseWeather`,
  MTB-roll an occasional temporary switch to `burstWeather`" — Forge points
  the temporary state at something WORSE (`RUT_BoilingRain` + scald damage);
  this def points it at something CALMER (vanilla `Clear`, confirmed real:
  `Core/Defs/WeatherDefs/Weathers.xml`, "A clear day. No penalties or
  modifiers."), with `scaldDamageDef` left unset so the burst carries no
  damage at all — the "still day" the spec asks for, literally implemented,
  zero new C#. No design ambiguity forced this choice: the spec already
  named the sheet's own "still day" beat, this is an engineering route to
  it that didn't exist as a reusable generic on 2026-09-13 but does now.

  Wired onto RUT_TheScald via a MayRequire-gated PatchOperationAdd
  (Patches/RUT_ScaldSteamLock_BiomeWiring.xml, unchanged), not a direct XML
  edit to the BiomeDef — a plain <li>RUT_ScaldSteamLock</li> baked into
  RUT_TheScald.xml's biomeMapConditions would be a dangling cross-reference
  if mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards is ever absent from the active mod
  list (same caution FEVER_WOOD_MECHANICS_1's continuation pass already
  applied to this exact file family, for the same reason).
  canBePermanent stays true: BiomeDef.biomeMapConditions entries are always
  made permanent by the engine (BiomeConditionMapComponent.MapGenerated ->
  GameConditionMaker.MakeConditionPermanent), required for a permanent
  condition to pass WeatherPulseExtension's own ConfigErrors too.

  Tuning (all INVENTED, no figure in the sheet): burstMtbHours 96 (mean 4
  in-game days between still days — rare, per §9's own "a still day", not a
  routine lull); burstDurationMinutesRange 720~1440 (12-24 in-game hours —
  long enough to actually show the wrecks per §9's own framing, short
  enough that the boil's breath is still the norm). flashWindowHours
  AfterBurstStart is required >0 by WeatherPulseExtension's own
  ConfigErrors but is INERT here: RUT_TheScald carries no
  RM_MapComponent_FlashCycle (that's Forge's own flash-growth mechanic),
  so `StartBurst`'s `GetComponent<RM_MapComponent_FlashCycle>()` lookup
  no-ops every time (confirmed by reading RM_GameCondition_WeatherPulse.
  StartBurst in full) — set to 1 rather than 0 only because 0 fails that
  ConfigErrors check.

  No damage/hediff/rot/plant-kill/density fields exist on this class at
  all (WeatherPulseExtension has no such fields) — the sheet is explicit
  the steam itself is clean; only the water burns.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <GameConditionDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_ScaldSteamLock</defName>
    <conditionClass>RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_GameCondition_WeatherPulse</conditionClass>
    <label>the boil's breath</label>
    <description>Standing steam over the Scald, endless and clean — it never rains here. Rarely, for a day at a time, the breath itself stills.</description>
    <canBePermanent>true</canBePermanent>
    <allowUnderground>true</allowUnderground>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.WeatherPulseExtension">
        <baseWeather>RUT_ScaldSteam</baseWeather>
        <burstWeather>Clear</burstWeather>
        <burstMtbHours>96</burstMtbHours>
        <burstDurationMinutesRange>720~1440</burstDurationMinutesRange>
        <flashWindowHoursAfterBurstStart>1</flashWindowHoursAfterBurstStart>
      </li>
      <!-- Mod Settings gate: Terminal Biomes' S1 steam-sky toggle. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_MechanicGateExtension">
        <gateKey>Scald.S1</gateKey>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </GameConditionDef>

</Defs>
